clude the breach written with Joe  Sutton and Catherine fellow about  Hurricane Katrina and wig-out about a  family of New York drag queens his  latest play choirboy was produced at the  Manhattan Theatre Club he is a graduate  of the Yale School of Drama the prize  citation for Terrell Alvin McCraney  reads tell Evan McQueen e's  working-class characters inhabit an  extraordinary mythic universe speaking  of poetic language through which we  grasp the spiritual stature of embattled  people congratulations to  Naomi Wallace is an American playwright  living in England  throughout her celebrated and incendiary  career Wallace has explored the role of  politics and power in shaping human  experience be it 17th century London  during the Great Plague in one flee  spare among black communists organizers  in 1930s Alabama things of dry hours or  in the parallel drama's of the Vietnam  and Gulf Wars in the heart of America  though her work can be dark and almost  brutal in its vision Tony Kushner  maintains that Wallace is outrageously  optimistic she seems to believe that the  world can change  she certainly writes as she intends to  set it on fire  her most recent play the liquid plane  won the 2012 horton Foote prize for the  most promising new American play and had  its world premiere at the Oregon  Shakespeare Festival in July the prize  citation for now me Wallace reads now  Lee Wallace mines historical situations  in plays that are muscular devastating  and unwavering no  congratulations in the gesture  so I have to just say something personal  many of you know I'm a psychologist but  I have a brother who's an associate  artistic director of a theatre the San  Diego rep theatre and I sent him a  little note about our three playwrights  who won last night and he wrote me back  this a few civ note saying he just  couldn't believe who we were honoring  and he wished he could fly in and he  went on and on like this I I was just  really thrilled that I could impress my 